at are members of DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic ('pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances ... using any highway for purposes of travel')."},{"span":"s10","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'using the intersection' is the party's footprint overlapping the intersection the subject approaches or occupies (rel.occupies 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'; st.intersection 'the region where two roadways meet', not a stand-in for a crosswalk)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s6","standard":"the right-of-way (DEF-NRS-484A-210: 'approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other')","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: the danger of a crash exists where, under constant velocities, the centres of the subject and the party approach within the conflict horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) to a centre distance below the conflict clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance), which reads the direction, the speed and the proximity of both together","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"There are an intersection i (st.intersection), a carrier c (st.travel_region) entering i (st.lane_enters(c, i)) and a traffic signal d (dev.traffic_signal) governing c (dev.governs(d, c)) such that d displays green_arrow(dir) for some dir among left, right and u_turn and no other state at the observation, and the subject, a member of traffic and a vehicle, either occupies c (rel.occupies(subject, c)) or occupies i and has occupied i continuously since an observation at which it occupied