lays green_arrow(left) alone; it turns left at 6 m/s while a pedestrian walks in the crosswalk marking the entrance of the cross street's approach (st.entrance_of); prim.closest_approach_within holds with a closest centre distance of 1.0 m in 1.5 s, and the subject keeps moving."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject halts (kin.speed 0) short of the crosswalk until the pedestrian has crossed, then completes its turn with no closest approach below the clearance within the horizon."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The signal governing the subject's approach displays circular_red."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The subject turns at a signalized intersection whose signal states are not observed by the source.","masked":["dev.traffic_signal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"On the green left arrow alone the subject turns left; no other road user is in the scene."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of tracked-object kinematics in driving datasets and simulators"},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"traffic conflict technique (Hydén; time-to-collision thresholds of 1.5 to 3 s)"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width","source":"AASHTO passenger-car design vehicle dimensions"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}

