at are members of DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic ('pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances ... using any highway for purposes of travel')."},{"span":"s10","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'using the intersection' is the party's footprint overlapping the intersection the subject approaches or occupies (rel.occupies 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'; st.intersection 'the region where two roadways meet', not a stand-in for a crosswalk)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s6","standard":"the right-of-way (DEF-NRS-484A-210: 'approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other')","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: the danger of a crash exists where, under constant velocities, the centres of the subject and the party approach within the conflict horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) to a centre distance below the conflict clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance), which reads the direction, the speed and the proximity of both together","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"There are an intersection i (st.intersection), a carrier c (st.travel_region) entering i (st.lane_enters(c, i)) and a traffic signal d (dev.traffic_signal) governing c (dev.governs(d, c)) such that d displays green_arrow(dir) for some dir among left, right and u_turn and no other state at the observation, and the subject, a member of traffic and a vehicle, either occupies c (rel.occupies(subject, c)) or occupies i and has occupied i continuously since an observation at which it occupied c (rel.occupies(subject, i) since rel.occupies(subject, c)).","obligation":"Re-binding i, c and d with the whole selection of the applicability: for every road user u other than the subject that either is a pedestrian (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian) occupying a crosswalk x (st.crosswalk) marking the entrance (st.entrance_of(x, c2)) of some carrier c2 entering i (st.lane_enters(c2, i)), or is a member of traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) occupying i: it is not the case that the subject moves (kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance) while either prim.closest_approach_within(subject, u; p.conflict_horizon) holds with prim.closest_approach_distance(subject, u; p.conflict_horizon) below p.conflict_centre_clearance, or rel.contact(subject, u) holds.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s8","why":"'lawfully' is not read: the words name no rule whose verdict decides the pedestrian's lawfulness, so every pedestrian within is protected. 'the adjacent crosswalk' — the words leave open which crosswalk the turning traffic crosses, since its exit leg is not known before the turn ends — is read as every crosswalk marking the entrance of a carrier into the same intersection; the danger-of-crash bound selects the one the subject's path meets.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"s10","why":"'lawfully' is not read: the words name no rule whose verdict decides the other traffic's lawfulness, so every member of traffic within the intersection is protected; the rule reaches further than the words only where that presence is unlawful.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"s6","why":"Direction, speed and proximity are read together through the constant-velocity closest approach of the centres; a change of speed or direction ahead is not anticipated.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"The subject vehicle occupies an approach lane whose dev.traffic_signal displays green_arrow(left) alone; it turns left at 6 m/s while a pedestrian walks in the crosswalk marking the entrance of the cross street's approach (st.entrance_of); prim.closest_approach_within holds with a closest centre distance of 1.0 m in 1.5 s, and the subject keeps moving."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject halts (kin.speed 0) short of the crosswalk until the pedestrian has crossed, then completes its turn with no closest approach below the clearance within the horizon."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The signal governing the subject's approach displays circular_red."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The subject turns at a signalized intersection whose signal states are not observed by the source.","masked":["dev.traffic_signal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"On the green left arrow alone the subject turns left; no other road user is in the scene."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of tracked-object kinematics in driving datasets and simulators"},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"traffic conflict technique (Hydén; time-to-collision thresholds of 1.5 to 3 s)"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width","source":"AASHTO passenger-car design vehicle dimensions"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}

