for some dir among left, right and u_turn at the observation, and the subject, a member of traffic and a vehicle, either occupies c (rel.occupies(subject, c)) or occupies i and has occupied i continuously since an observation at which it occupied c (rel.occupies(subject, i) since rel.occupies(subject, c)).","obligation":"Re-binding i, c and d with the whole selection of the applicability: for every road user u other than the subject that either is a pedestrian (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian) occupying a crosswalk x (st.crosswalk) marking the entrance (st.entrance_of(x, c2)) of some carrier c2 entering i (st.lane_enters(c2, i)), or is a member of traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) occupying i: it is not the case that the subject moves (kin.speed above p.halt_speed_tolerance) while either prim.closest_approach_within(subject, u; p.conflict_horizon) holds with prim.closest_approach_distance(subject, u; p.conflict_horizon) below p.conflict_centre_clearance, or rel.contact(subject, u) holds.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s7","why":"The right-of-way is owed to the parties s9 to s13 name; their 'lawfully' (twice) is not read: the words name no rule whose verdict decides a party's lawfulness, so every pedestrian within an adjacent crosswalk and every member of traffic within the intersection is owed it; the rule reaches further than the words only where that presence is unlawful. 'an adjacent crosswalk' is any crosswalk marking the entrance of a carrier into the same intersection; 'at the time the signal is exhibited' is every observation at which the circular green with a green turn arrow is displayed. Direction, speed and proximity are read together through the constant-velocity closest approach of the centres.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"The subject vehicle occupies an approach lane whose dev.traffic_signal displays circular_green with green_arrow(right); it turns right at 6 m/s while a pedestrian walks in the crosswalk marking the entrance of the cross street's approach (st.entrance_of); prim.closest_approach_within holds with a closest centre distance of 1.0 m in 1.5 s, and the subject keeps moving."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject halts (kin.speed 0) short of the crosswalk until the pedestrian has crossed, then completes its turn with no closest approach below the clearance within the horizon."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The signal governing the subject's approach displays circular_green alone, with no arrow."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The subject turns at a signalized intersection whose signal states are not observed by the source.","masked":["dev.traffic_signal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"On circular green with green_arrow(left) the subject turns left; no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"On circular green with green_arrow(left) the subject turns left at 7 m/s toward a cyclist (a member of traffic) already within the intersection; prim.closest_approach_within holds with a closest centre distance of 1.2 m in 1.0 s."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of tracked-object kinematics in driving datasets and simulators"},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"traffic conflict technique (Hydén; time-to-collision thresholds of 1.5 to 3 s)"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at 